# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# AI provider configuration
#
# Keys are ONLY ever read server-side (in lib/ai/*, all `server-only`) and are
# never exposed to the client. Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill it in.
#
# Two providers: DeepSeek (much cheaper, the default when its key is set) and
# Anthropic/Claude. Set at least one key. With both set, students can switch
# between them on the setup page, and Claude reads any photo DeepSeek can't.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# DeepSeek API key (starts with sk-...). Server-side only.
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=

# Your Anthropic API key (starts with sk-ant-...). Server-side only. Keep it
# alongside DeepSeek as the photo backup, or on its own to run only on Claude.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Optional: vision-capable model id. Defaults to claude-sonnet-5 (cheaper).
# Set to claude-opus-5 for more headroom.
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Optional: the default provider, `deepseek` or `anthropic`. Unset = DeepSeek
# when DEEPSEEK_API_KEY is set, else Anthropic. The setup-page switch overrides
# it per student, for any provider whose key is set.
# AI_PROVIDER=deepseek

# Optional DeepSeek settings. deepseek-flash takes photos; deepseek-v4-pro is
# stronger but pricier and (reportedly) text-only, so photos would go to Claude.
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-flash
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com
# DEEPSEEK_VISION=off   # send every photo to Claude instead of trying DeepSeek

# Optional, experimental: question detection (the crop step's question boxes).
# Both are off until `npm run eval -- --kind detect` shows they help.
# DETECT_PROVIDER pins detection to one provider (needs its key), whoever
# tutors; the privacy page follows it. Unset = the tutor's provider.
# DETECT_GRID=on draws a labelled coordinate grid on the photo sent for
# detection (never on the one the student sees) to steady the boxes.
# DETECT_PROVIDER=anthropic
# DETECT_GRID=on

# Optional: shared access code. When set, visitors must enter it before using
# the app (protects your API credits on a public URL). Unset = no gate.
# Set this in the Vercel dashboard for a hosted deploy.
# ACCESS_CODE=

# Optional: several access codes, each with its own expiry. Comma- or
# newline-separated `code:expiry`, where expiry is YYYY-MM-DD (works through the
# end of that day, UTC), a full ISO time, or `never`. Works alongside
# ACCESS_CODE. Edit + redeploy to add, cancel or extend a code; it applies to
# people already logged in. A list where nothing parses keeps the gate CLOSED.
# Set ACCESS_SECRET too, or every edit to this list logs everyone out.
# ACCESS_CODES=maya2026:2026-10-31, studygroup:2026-12-20, teacher:never

# Optional: key for signing the access cookie. The cookie holds an HMAC of the
# code, never the code itself. Unset = the code is used as the key, which still
# keeps it out of the cookie; set a long random value to separate the two.
# Changing either ACCESS_CODE or this logs everyone out once.
# ACCESS_SECRET=

# Optional: per-IP rate limit for the AI routes, requests per minute.
# Defaults to 30/min. A burst brake so one visitor can't drain the key.
# Tune it here (no code change) — raise for heavier use, lower to be stricter.
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_MIN=30

# Optional: per-IP DAILY cap on the AI routes, counted over 24 hours. Defaults
# to 150 — roughly 10-15 photographed problems' worth of calls. This is the real
# spend ceiling; the per-minute limit is only a burst brake.
# RATE_LIMIT_PER_DAY=150

# Optional but needed for the caps above to be global on Vercel: a shared
# Upstash Redis store (Vercel → Storage → Upstash adds these for you; the
# KV_REST_API_URL / KV_REST_API_TOKEN names work too). Unset = counts live in
# each server instance's memory and reset on a cold start.
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=

# Optional debug flags (off by default; safe to toggle in Vercel):
#   DEBUG_TOKENS=1  logs per-call token usage + cache hits to the server console.
#   DEBUG_ERRORS=1  includes the underlying error detail in API error responses
#                   (so you can see the real cause from the browser). Turn off
#                   again afterward — it exposes error internals.
# DEBUG_TOKENS=
# DEBUG_ERRORS=

# Optional: let students pick DeepSeek or Claude in Settings (needs both keys).
# Off by default: DeepSeek answers and Claude is only its automatic backup,
# because Claude costs far more. The privacy page follows this setting.
# TUTOR_SWITCH=on
